From: KB2UKA <kb2uka@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: reset: match optional SMC state cells

The current macsmc-reboot driver accepts absent state cells and guards each
cell access. Its comment says, "Without this, the device will just reboot."
It makes shutdown_flag optional in case newer hardware no longer needs it;
that exception has not been verified on J713 Abbey.

Keep the four-cell layout when supplied, but allow the pair of properties
to be omitted. This covers the no-cells and all-four-cells cases, not every
partial-cell combination tolerated by the driver. Abbey offsets have not
been established; this does not copy another PMIC family's offsets or
assert stay-off behavior.

This is unapplied, unvalidated source guidance. It was not used to build
the candidate DTB and does not alter the kernel binary or its ABI.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/apple,smc-reboot.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/apple,smc-reboot.yaml
@@ -35,6 +35,8 @@
+dependencies:
+  nvmem-cells: [ nvmem-cell-names ]
+  nvmem-cell-names: [ nvmem-cells ]
+
 required:
   - compatible
-  - nvmem-cells
-  - nvmem-cell-names

 additionalProperties: false
